    <string name="changelog__dialog_title" comment="Title of the what's-new dialog shown after an update">What\'s new</string>
    <string name="changelog__view_all" comment="Button that opens the full changelog/releases page online">View all changes</string>
    <string name="changelog__intro" comment="Brief intro line at the top of the what's-new dialog, before the per-version notes">Dictate has been updated. Here\'s what\'s new:</string>
    <string name="changelog__version_header" comment="Header shown above one release's notes. {version} is e.g. 4.0.0">Version {version}</string>
    <string name="changelog__donate" comment="Tappable invitation to donate, shown at the bottom of the what's-new dialog">Enjoying Dictate? Tap here to support development ♥</string>
    <!-- Per-release notes. To announce a new version, add a changelog__vX_Y_Z string here and a matching
         entry in DictateChangelog.kt. changelog__current holds the notes for the initial 4.0.0 release. -->
    <string name="changelog__current" comment="What's-new text for the 4.0.0 release. One change per line.">• Brand-new keyboard: Dictate now ships as a full multi-language layout keyboard with a dedicated mic key that opens the voice panel.\n• Bring your own AI: pick any OpenAI-compatible provider and enter your API key under Settings → Dictate.\n• Smart formatting and rewording powered by your chosen model.\n• Your settings from the previous Dictate app are imported automatically.</string>
    <string name="changelog__v4_1_0" comment="What's-new text for the 4.1.0 release. One change per line.">• New: search emoji right from the keyboard.\n• New transcription provider: Soniox.\n• Re-insert your last dictation, and recover recordings interrupted when the keyboard closed.\n• The prompt bar now refreshes live — long-press a prompt to edit it.\n• The AI providers screen now shows both your active transcription and rewording providers.\n• Bigger, easier-to-hit record button.\n• Fixes: a support prompt could get stuck and block the bar in some languages; backup no longer fails when prompts, keyboard or theme are selected; saved API keys are kept when upgrading.</string>
    <string name="changelog__v5_0_0" comment="What\'s-new text for the 5.0.0 release. One change per line.">• NEW: Glide typing — swipe across the keys to type whole words, with per-language dictionaries that download on demand. 👆\n• NEW: Word suggestions &amp; autocorrect — typos get fixed automatically and the word you typed stays one tap away. ✨\n• NEW: Real-time transcription — watch your words appear as you speak, with OpenAI, Deepgram, Soniox, AssemblyAI and ElevenLabs. ⚡\n• NEW: Three more transcription providers — ElevenLabs Scribe, Deepgram and AssemblyAI. ☁️\n• NEW: Classic dictation layout — the keyboard-free voice screen from Dictate 3 is back, locked or just a swipe away. 🎙️\n• NEW: Community prompt library — browse and share rewording prompts. 📚\n• NEW: Dictation statistics with milestones. 📊\n• NEW: Offline model NVIDIA Parakeet, plus a silence filter that skips empty recordings. 📴\n• More: a steadier floating button, reasoning-effort control, haptic feedback, a new E-Reader theme and dozens of fixes. 🛠️</string>
    <string name="changelog__v4_3_0" comment="What\'s-new text for the 4.3.0 release. One change per line.">• NEW: On-device transcription — dictate completely offline. No internet needed and nothing leaves your phone. Download a speech model once in Settings ▸ Dictate ▸ Providers. 📴\n• NEW: Wear OS keyboard — dictate straight from your watch, through your phone or fully on its own. ⌚\n• NEW: Find &amp; replace rules — automatically fix recurring words, names or phrases in every transcript. Set them up in Settings ▸ Dictate ▸ Custom mappings. 🔁\n• NEW: Single-call mode — let one capable AI model transcribe and format in a single request, faster and often cheaper. Turn it on per provider. ⚡\n• NEW: Smartbar actions to jump back to your previous keyboard or open the system keyboard picker. ⌨️\n• The keyboard\'s accent color now follows the color you pick in Settings ▸ Theme. 🎨\n• Added an optional undo button to the floating dictation button. ↩️\n• Various fixes and stability improvements. 🛠️</string>
    <string name="changelog__v4_2_0" comment="What's-new text for the 4.2.0 release. One change per line.">• NEW: Floating dictation button — dictate straight into any app, even when another keyboard is active. Pick from three styles (Pill, Ring, Orb), watch a live waveform while you speak, drag it anywhere with edge-snapping, set its color and size, and long-press to reword. Turn it on in Settings ▸ Dictate ▸ Floating button.\n• NEW: Google Gemini — bring your own AI Studio API key for both transcription and rewording.\n• Prompts now appear in an always-on row above the keys by default.\n• More reliable text insertion across apps, including browsers and other keyboards.</string>
    <string name="changelog__v4_1_1" comment="What's-new text for the 4.1.1 release. One change per line.">• Fix: the accent color could appear green on some devices — keys and buttons are back to the Dictate blue.</string>

